<title>USA: Leslie-ADM soybean production survey by state.</title>
<headline>Leslie-ADM soybean production survey by state.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following tables contain state-by-state soybean production estimates published in the Leslie-ADM Investor Services Crop survey.</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION (IN 000'S BUSHELS)</p>
<p>	 LESLIE 10/1/96  USDA 9/1/96  USDA 1995</p>
<p> PENN	   12,825	 12,540	 9,450</p>
<p> OHIO	  152,660	143,680     153,140</p>
<p> INDIANA     198,320	187,600     194,220</p>
<p> ILLINOIS    374,300	364,450     373,450</p>
<p> MICHIGAN     52,480	 52,480	59,600</p>
<p> WISCONSIN    33,930	 33,930	34,400</p>
<p> MINN	  206,500	212,400     232,000</p>
<p> IOWA	  415,800	415,800     398,180</p>
<p> MISSOURI    145,800	141,750     130,500</p>
<p> N DAKOTA     24,600	 24,600	18,560</p>
<p> S DAKOTA     82,150	 84,800	75,000</p>
<p> NEBRASKA    132,440	132,440	99,450</p>
<p> KANSAS	 70,000	 68,000	51,250</p>
<p> MARYLAND     16,800	 15,840	11,730</p>
<p> VIRGINIA     16,320	 15,360	11,280</p>
<p> N CAROLINA   33,600	 37,200	26,750</p>
<p> S CAROLINA   15,120	 14,040	12,720</p>
<p> GEORGIA	 9,750	 10,140	 8,370</p>
<p> KENTUCKY     44,840	 42,480	41,400</p>
<p> TENNESSEE    39,100	 36,800	34,560</p>
<p> ALABAMA	 9,135	  8,820	 5,400</p>
<p> MISS	   45,500	 47,250	37,800</p>
<p> ARKANSAS    108,000	108,000	86,700</p>
<p> LOUISIANA    33,600	 32,550	26,000</p>
<p> TEXAS	   8,370	  7,830	 6,000</p>
<p> OTHERS	 20,389	 18,725	13,924</p>
<p> TOTAL     2,302,329    2,269,505   2,177,000</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720)</p>
